andpulled-noodle"],["Harbor City Restaurant","dish/harbor-city-restaurant"],["Heichinrou","dish/heichinrou"],["HK Cafe","dish/hk-cafe"],["Hog maw","dish/hog-maw"],["Hong dou tang","dish/hong-dou-tang"],["Hot dry noodles","dish/hot-dry-noodles"],["Hot pot","dish/hot-pot"],["Hotcha (company)","dish/hotcha-company"]]}]},"dish/keumamah":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/keumamah","n":"Keumamah","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Keumamah is a traditional dried fish in Acehnese cuisine, usually made skipjack or tuna. Keumamah is also known as \"wood fish\", due to its hardness. It is preserved through several processes, from cleaning the fish to boiling, drying, and storing; therefore, keumamah can be stored for years, provided it is kept dry and free from moisture."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-keumamah"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keumamah"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Acehnese cuisine","cuisine/acehnese-cuisine"],["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":7,"links":[["Bird's eye chili","ingredient/bird-s-eye-chili"],["Black pepper","ingredient/black-pepper"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Skipjack tuna","ingredient/skipjack-tuna"],["Thunnus tonggol","ingredient/thunnus-tonggol"],["Tuna","ingredient/tuna"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","ref":"site/dailycookingquest-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Acehnese cuisine","links":[["Meuseukat","dish/meuseukat"],["Mie aceh","dish/mie-aceh"],["Mie caluk","dish/mie-caluk"],["Timphan","dish/timphan"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/e/e4/Keumamah.jpg/500px-Keumamah.jpg","w":500,"h":281,"by":"Si Gam","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Keumamah.jpg"}},"ingredient/krupuk-kulit":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/krupuk-kulit","n":"Krupuk kulit","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Krupuk kulit is a traditional Indonesian cattle skin krupuk (cracker). It is traditionally made from the soft inner skin of cattle (cow or water buffalo) which is diced and sun-dried until it hardens and loses most of its water content. The diced and dried skins are later fried in ample hot cooking oil until they expand similarly with bubbles and yield a crispy texture. This fried cattle skin is then sealed in vacuum plastic bags to ensure and prolong its crispiness."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-krupuk-kulit"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krupuk_kulit"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Krechek","dish/krechek"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Cowhide","ingredient/cowhide"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/9/94/Kerupuk_kulit.JPG/500px-Kerupuk_kulit.JPG","w":500,"h":443,"by":"Midori","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kerupuk_kulit.JPG"}},"dish/ma-amoul":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/ma-amoul","n":"Ma'amoul","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Arab cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Ma'amoul is a filled cookie made with semolina flour and butter. Originating in the Arab world, the filling can be made with dried fruits like figs, dates, or nuts such as pistachios, walnuts, and occasionally almonds or cheese."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-ma-amoul"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ma'amoul"}],"sectio