ite/manusmenu-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"manusmenu.com","note":"Italian-born home cook Manuela sharing classic family and regional Italian dishes.","url":"https://www.manusmenu.com/about/about-this-site","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Italian cuisine","links":[["8½ Otto e Mezzo Bombana","dish/8-otto-e-mezzo-bombana"],["A16 (restaurant)","dish/a16-restaurant"],["Acquacotta","dish/acquacotta"],["Agliata","dish/agliata"],["Agnolotti","dish/agnolotti"],["Alfredo alla Scrofa","dish/alfredo-alla-scrofa"],["Alioto's","dish/alioto-s"],["Amalfi's Italian Restaurant","dish/amalfi-s-italian-restaurant"],["Amato's","dish/amato-s"],["Angelo's Civita Farnese","dish/angelo-s-civita-farnese"],["Antica Pizzeria Port'Alba","dish/antica-pizzeria-port-alba"],["Antico Pizza","dish/antico-pizza"],["Antipasto","dish/antipasto"],["Arancini","dish/arancini"],["ASK Italian","dish/ask-italian"],["Asti (restaurant)","dish/asti-restaurant"],["Ava Gene's","dish/ava-gene-s"],["Bamonte's","dish/bamonte-s"],["Bar del Corso","dish/bar-del-corso"],["Barbetta","dish/barbetta"],["Barbuto (restaurant)","dish/barbuto-restaurant"],["Bella Italia","dish/bella-italia"],["Beppi's Restaurant","dish/beppi-s-restaurant"],["Bertucci's","dish/bertucci-s"],["BiCE Ristorante","dish/bice-ristorante"],["Biscotti","dish/biscotti"],["Black' Smith","dish/black-smith"],["Bocca di Lupo","dish/bocca-di-lupo"],["Bolinhos de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalhau"],["Bombolone","dish/bombolone"],["Buca di Beppo","dish/buca-di-beppo"],["Budino","dish/budino"],["Buona","dish/buona"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Caffé Vittoria","dish/caffe-vittoria"],["Camille's (Providence, Rhode Island)","dish/camille-s-providence-rhode-island"],["Campisi's Egyptian Restaurant","dish/campisi-s-egyptian-restaurant"],["Cannelloni","dish/cannelloni"],["Capellini","dish/capellini"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/8/88/Numero_28_East_Village_Store_Front.jpg/500px-Numero_28_East_Village_Store_Front.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Sablizzard","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Numero_28_East_Village_Store_Front.jpg"}},"ingredient/lung":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/lung","n":"Lung","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["The lungs are the primary organs of the respiratory system in many animals, including humans. In mammals and most other tetrapods, two lungs are located near the backbone on either side of the heart. Their function in the respiratory system is to extract oxygen from the atmosphere and transfer it into the bloodstream, and to release carbon dioxide from the bloodstream into the atmosphere, in a process of gas exchange. Respiration is driven by different muscular systems in different species. Mammals, reptiles and birds use their musculoskeletal systems to support and foster breathing. In early tetrapods, air was driven into the lungs by the pharyngeal muscles via buccal pumping, a mechanism still seen in amphibians. In humans, the primary muscle that drives breathing is the diaphragm. The lungs also provide airflow that makes vocalisation including speech possible."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-lung"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lung"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Sicilian cuisine","cuisine/sicilian-cuisine",[["Pani câ meusa","dish/pani-ca-meusa"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Spleen","ingredient/spleen"]]}]},"dish/pkhali":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/pkhali","n":"Pkhali","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Georgian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Pkhali is a traditional Georgian dish of chopped and minced vegetables, made of cabbage, eggplant, spinach, beans, beets and combined with ground walnuts, vinegar, onions, garlic, and herbs. Pkhali is also called mkhali. The common ingredient of all variations of pkhali is puréed walnut sauce. In Georgian restaurants, pkhali is usually served in three types: spinach, beetroot and white beans."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-pkhali"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pkhali"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Georgian cuisine","cuisine/georgian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":9,"links":[["Beta","ingredient/beta"],["Brassica","ingredient/brassica"],["Eggplant","ingredient/eggplant"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Juglans regia","ingredient/juglans-regia"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Phaseolus","ingredient/phaseolus"],["Spinacia","ingredient/spinacia"],["Vinegar","ingredient/vinegar"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Georgian Recipes","ref":"site/georgianrecipes-net","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"georgianrecipes.net","note":"Recipe site dedicated to traditional Georgian dishes.","url":"https://georgianrecipes.net/about-georgian-recipes","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Georgian cuisine","links":[["Achma","dish/achma"],["Ajika","dish/ajika"],["Akhasheni","dish/akhasheni"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Chakapuli","dish/chakapuli"],["Chakhokhbili","dish/chakhokhbili"],["Chashushuli","dish/chashushuli"],["Chicken tabaka","dish/chicken-tabaka"],["Churchkhela","dish/churchkhela"],["Dambalkhacho","dish/dambalkhacho"],["Eggplant jam","dish/eggplant-jam"],["Gozinaki","dish/gozinaki"],["Khachapuri","dish/khachapuri"],["Kharcho","dish/kharcho"],["Khash (dish)","dish/khash-dish"],["Khvanchkara","dish/khvanchkara"],["Kindzmarauli","dish/kindzmarauli"],["Kubdari","dish/kubdari"],["Kuchmachi","dish/kuchmachi"],["Kvass","dish/kvass"],["Lobiani","dish/lobiani"],["Mchadi","dish/mchadi"],["Mujuretuli","dish/mujuretuli"],["Nadugi","dish/nadugi"],["Nigvziani badrijani","dish/nigvziani-badrijani"],["Shkmeruli","dish/shkmeruli"],["Tsolikouri","dish/tsolikouri"],["Tvishi (wine)","dish/tvishi-wine"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/b/ba/Cabbage_pkhali.jpg/500px-Cabbage_pkhali.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Georgia About","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cabbage_pkhali.jpg"}},"ingredient/kidney":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/kidney","n":"Kidney","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["The human kidneys are two reddish-brown bean-shaped blood-filtering organs that are a multilobar, multipapillary form of mammalian kidneys, usually without signs of external lobulation. They are located on the left and right in the retroperitoneal space, and in adult humans are about 12 centimetres in length. They receive blood from the paired renal arteries; blood exits into the paired renal veins. Each kidney is attached to a ureter, a tube that carries excreted urine to the bladder."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-kidney"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kidney"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine",[["Rassolnik","dish/rassolnik"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Brine","ingredient/brine"],["Kidneys as food","ingredient/kidneys-as-food"],["Liver as food","ingredient/liver-as-food"],["Pearl barley","ingredient/pearl-barley"],["Pickled cucumber","ingredient/pickled-cucumber"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/d6/Blausen_0592_KidneyAnatomy_01.png/500px-Blausen_0592_KidneyAnatomy_01.png","w":500,"h":375,"by":"BruceBlaus. When using this image in external sources it can be cited as: Blausen.com…","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blausen_0592_KidneyAnatomy_01.png"}},"dish/sushi-taro":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/sushi-taro","n":"Sushi Taro","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],